{#- testing/remote_harness/templates/macros/registry_ingress.j2 -- the ONE pre-parse registry admission of every harness
    entry (codex-tick755 OPEN-S17-REG-EXPECTED-ID). Every name, path, selector, word and text is an atom of the
    ingress declaration d (testing/remote_harness/registry_ingress.decl.yml); the macro holds none of its own.
    (1) the launch envelope (the envelope_transport var, passed in) names the selected transport at d.transport_selector;
        it is a declared transport, its var is supplied, every other non-envelope transport var is absent, and the
        envelope identity equals the selected identity (records-transport-custody-01). The selected identity value
        (walked along its declared path)
        fully matches d.digest.regex. The value is read AMBIENTLY: lookup(ansible.builtin.vars) resolves the declared
        var among the variables of the calling render (play variables overlaid by the entry template_vars), so this
        macro is NOT argument-pure; the set of transport vars is bound to the admitted ABI after the parse
        (admit_loader_source). (2) custody before use: every component of d.registry_rel below root is not a symbolic
        link and the path is a regular file; a Vault envelope is refused before the read. (3) the file is captured
        ONCE (file lookup, rstrip and lstrip both false, no transformation); a capture holding a surrogate escape
        (d.capture.undecodable_regex) is refused; then its d.digest.algorithm digest is compared with the admitted
        value BEFORE any parse. (4) the SAME captured text is parsed ONCE, macro-local. (5) each d.protected_lists list
        is a non-empty list, and no protected name (those lists + d.protected_extra) is among the supplied names.
        (6) it returns identity, transport key, d and the d.slice node under the d.output words. A failure renders an
        undefined key of d.diagnostics whose name is the declared text plus its detail, which stops the render with
        that text (no code exists before the registry).
    (1b) companions (records-c1-framework-27, codex-tick821 REP-D1): every d.companions entry is supplied, passes its
        test, is non-empty and equals the envelope value at its path; companions are not transports and never enter
        the transport exclusivity loop. A companion var that is also a protected name refuses after the lists check.
    Bytes vs text: the file loader decodes strictly as UTF-8 but, on undecodable bytes, falls back to surrogate
    escaping (the hash filter would then re-encode the escapes to the original bytes), and it decrypts a Vault file.
    So the macro admits only valid-UTF-8, non-Vault plaintext: for that text the UTF-8 encoding of the capture equals
    the file bytes (LF, CRLF, a BOM and leading / trailing whitespace are kept), and the digest is of those bytes. -#}
{#- [op1d text, kept for lineage; its identity-var selection is SUPERSEDED by the op1e block below]
    op1d (records-route-op1d-01 OP1D-RI-01; codex 916 Q-OP1C-PROJECTOR-ENVELOPE): CARRIER SELECTION. Every atom is a word of
    the ingress declaration d, under the proposed C1 node d.carriers (OWED-C1-OP1D-INGRESS-CARRIERS) and d.atoms:
    d.carriers.projector = {identity: {var, path}, entry_rel, transport}; d.carriers.words = {envelope, projector};
    d.diagnostics.carrier; d.output.carrier / d.output.entry_identity. The PROJECTOR carrier is selected by the externally
    admitted ENTRY IDENTITY (the projector identity var among the supplied names, its value a full-match digest equal to
    the measured bytes of the declared projector entry rel under the same custody as the registry), never by envelope
    absence, a flag, a record stage or a quoted rel; under it the envelope var refuses (mixed carriers) and the
    selected transport is d.carriers.projector.transport (the transport exclusivity loop below is unchanged). Without
    the identity var, the ENVELOPE branch is the base text verbatim. The running entry is bound to that identity after
    the resolve (admit_record_free_entry carrier join); an ordinary entry under the projector carrier refuses there. -#}
{#- op1e SR918-CARRIER-SELECTION-ORDER (records-route-op1e-01 OP1E-RI-01; codex 918): the op1d selection by the PRESENCE of a
    supplied projector identity var is WITHDRAWN. The carrier is selected by the ACTUAL EXECUTING ENTRY, bound before any
    registry capture or parse: px holds iff the executing play (Ansible magic variables of the running playbook, named by
    d.carriers.projector.select {play_var, dir_var}; they outrank every supplied name, so no extra-var can set them)
    has the declared projector play name (select.play_name) and runs from the declared projector entry's directory below
    root. The EXTERNAL X2 ADMISSION (d.carriers.projector.admission {var, fields}; the mapping MAIN admitted and B carries)
    must be supplied iff px: an ordinary entry supplied with it (or with a valid projector digest inside it) refuses, and
    a projector entry without it refuses. Under px it must bind, before the registry is read: entry_rel = the declared
    projector entry rel; entry_sha256 = the measured bytes of that rel (registry custody); registry_sha256 = the selected
    cold transport identity (an altered entry / registry pair refuses); document_parse = the parse settings this render
    parsed the ingress declaration with (the top template reads them from the same admission). Its presence corroborates;
    it never selects. Under px the envelope var refuses (mixed carriers); without px the base envelope text holds. The
    later consistency rows (admit_cold_launch, admit_record_free_entry) stay as defense in depth. Residual: the exact
    executing FILE (beyond play name and directory) is bound by the X2 exec vector MAIN admits (playbook = entry_rel). -#}
{#- op1f (records-route-op1f-01 OP1F-RI-01; C1 s13 decl 29a1084a carriers / atoms / canonical_json, C1 FINAL shape; codex
    919 6db9d001): the shape is consumed as C1 declared it and no word is added. (a) The selector (select play_var /
    dir_var / play_name) and the play-name uniqueness rule (carriers.rules.play_name) are SUPPLEMENTARY CONSISTENCY
    CHECKS: they do not prove which file executes. The exact executing file (its measured path and bytes, with the
    registry identity, in the X2-admitted vector) is bound BEFORE LAUNCH by B's external first-invocation writer /
    verifier, which MAIN independently admits; this macro does not claim that binding. (b) The admission has five
    fields (+ companions): under the projector carrier every declared companion var is supplied, passes its test, is
    non-empty and equals the admission companions value for that var, and the admission companions keys are exactly
    the declared companion vars (no envelope). (c) Every carrier and companion refusal precedes the registry capture
    (carriers.rules.refuse_before). (d) Comparison options are d.canonical_json and constants are d.atoms (read from
    the declaration, returned unchanged as output.ingress). (e) caller_protected adds the admission var (caller-protected,
    not a reserved output). The admission document_parse is the document_channel.parse node of the X2-admitted registry
    bytes (MAIN's X2 admitter computes it); here it must equal the settings the render parsed with, the registry digest
    must equal admission registry_sha256 before the parse, and the post-parse parse_contract row reconciles that node. -#}
{#- op1g (records-route-op1g-01 OP1G-RI-01; C1 s15 decl 42600902 atoms.zero, C1-SR919): every integer comparison with
    zero reads d.atoms.zero and the pair count reads d.atoms.one + d.atoms.one; no other change. CPL-SR919B-MACRO-GATE
    (optional) is NOT taken: a pre-parse constant gate would need a diagnostics text the decl does not declare (a new
    word); ALS05 :246-295 validates the constants post-parse and the declaration bytes are digest-pinned. -#}
{%- macro registry_ingress(d, root, supplied, parse, envelope) -%}
{%- set ev = d.transports[d.envelope_transport].var -%}
{%- set pj = d.carriers.projector -%}
{%- set pa = pj.admission -%}
{%- set px = (lookup('ansible.builtin.vars', pj.select.play_var) == pj.select.play_name)
             and ((lookup('ansible.builtin.vars', pj.select.dir_var) | relpath(root)) == (pj.entry_rel | dirname)) -%}
{%- if px != (pa.var in supplied) or (px and ev in supplied) -%}{{ d.diagnostics[d.diagnostics.carrier ~ d.diagnostics.joiner ~ ([pa.var, ev] | to_json)] }}{%- endif -%}
{%- set sn = namespace(v=(pj.transport if px else envelope)) -%}
{%- if not px -%}
{%- for k in d.transport_selector -%}{%- set sn.v = sn.v[k] -%}{%- endfor -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- set tx = namespace(bad=d.atoms.empty_list) -%}
{%- for t in d.transports | dict2items -%}{%- if t.value.var != ev and ((t.key == sn.v) != (t.value.var in supplied)) -%}{%- set tx.bad = tx.bad + [t.key] -%}{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}
{%- if sn.v is not string or sn.v not in d.transports or (tx.bad | length) > d.atoms.zero -%}{{ d.diagnostics[d.diagnostics.transport ~ d.diagnostics.joiner ~ ([sn.v, tx.bad] | to_json)] }}{%- endif -%}
{%- set tr = d.transports[sn.v] -%}
{%- set ex = namespace(v=lookup('ansible.builtin.vars', tr.var)) -%}
{%- for k in tr.path -%}{%- set ex.v = ex.v[k] -%}{%- endfor -%}
{%- if ex.v is not string or ex.v is not match(d.digest.regex) -%}{{ d.diagnostics[d.diagnostics.expected ~ d.diagnostics.joiner ~ tr.var] }}{%- endif -%}
{%- if px -%}
{#- op1e: the external X2 admission binds the actual entry and registry identity BEFORE the registry capture below: exactly
    its declared fields; entry_rel is the declared projector entry rel; entry_sha256 a full-match digest equal to the
    bytes of that rel (reached without a symbolic link below root, a regular non-Vault plaintext UTF-8 file, captured
    once, both strips off); registry_sha256 equal to the selected cold transport identity; document_parse equal (type-
    exact) to the parse settings this render used -#}
{%- set xa = lookup('ansible.builtin.vars', pa.var) -%}
{%- if xa is not mapping or (xa.keys() | list | sort) != (pa.fields.values() | list | sort) -%}{{ d.diagnostics[d.diagnostics.carrier ~ d.diagnostics.joiner ~ ([pa.var] | to_json)] }}{%- endif -%}
{%- set pi = namespace(v=xa[pa.fields.entry_sha256]) -%}
{%- if pi.v is not string or pi.v is not match(d.digest.regex) -%}{{ d.diagnostics[d.diagnostics.expected ~ d.diagnostics.joiner ~ pa.var] }}{%- endif -%}
{%- if xa[pa.fields.entry_rel] != pj.entry_rel or xa[pa.fields.registry_sha256] != ex.v
      or (xa[pa.fields.document_parse] | to_json(**d.canonical_json)) != (parse | to_json(**d.canonical_json))
      or xa[pa.fields.companions] is not mapping
      or (xa[pa.fields.companions].keys() | list | sort) != (d.companions | dict2items | map(attribute='value') | map(attribute='var') | list | sort) -%}{{ d.diagnostics[d.diagnostics.carrier ~ d.diagnostics.joiner ~ ([pa.var, pa.fields] | to_json)] }}{%- endif -%}
{%- set pe = namespace(p=root, links=d.atoms.empty_list) -%}
{%- for c in pj.entry_rel.split(d.separator) -%}{%- set pe.p = pe.p ~ d.separator ~ c -%}{%- if pe.p is link -%}{%- set pe.links = pe.links + [c] -%}{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}
{%- if pe.links or pe.p is not file or pe.p is vaulted_file -%}{{ d.diagnostics[d.diagnostics.carrier ~ d.diagnostics.joiner ~ ([pj.entry_rel, pe.links] | to_json)] }}{%- endif -%}
{%- set pt = lookup('ansible.builtin.file', pe.p, rstrip=d.atoms.false_value, lstrip=d.atoms.false_value) -%}
{%- if pt is search(d.capture.undecodable_regex) or (pt | hash(d.digest.algorithm)) != pi.v -%}{{ d.diagnostics[d.diagnostics.carrier ~ d.diagnostics.joiner ~ ([pj.entry_rel, pa.var] | to_json)] }}{%- endif -%}
{%- else -%}
{%- set ei = namespace(v=envelope) -%}
{%- for k in d.transports[d.envelope_transport].path -%}{%- set ei.v = ei.v[k] -%}{%- endfor -%}
{%- if ei.v != ex.v -%}{{ d.diagnostics[d.diagnostics.envelope_identity ~ d.diagnostics.joiner ~ ([sn.v, tr.var] | to_json)] }}{%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- set cp = namespace(bad=d.atoms.empty_list) -%}
{%- for c in d.companions | dict2items -%}
{%- if px -%}
{#- op1f projector companions (closes HOLE-OP1D-PROJECTOR-COMPANIONS on the pre-parse side): supplied, of the declared test,
    non-empty and equal (typed) to the X2 admission companions value for that var (the admission keys were checked
    exact above); never from an envelope -#}
{%- if c.value.var not in supplied or ([lookup('ansible.builtin.vars', c.value.var), xa[pa.fields.companions][c.value.var]] | select(c.value.test) | list | length) != (d.atoms.one + d.atoms.one) or not lookup('ansible.builtin.vars', c.value.var)
      or (lookup('ansible.builtin.vars', c.value.var) | to_json(**d.canonical_json)) != (xa[pa.fields.companions][c.value.var] | to_json(**d.canonical_json)) -%}{%- set cp.bad = cp.bad + [c.key] -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- else -%}
{%- set cw = namespace(v=envelope) -%}
{%- for k in c.value.path -%}{%- set cw.v = cw.v[k] -%}{%- endfor -%}
{%- if c.value.var not in supplied or ([lookup('ansible.builtin.vars', c.value.var), cw.v] | select(c.value.test) | list | length) != (d.atoms.one + d.atoms.one) or (lookup('ansible.builtin.vars', c.value.var) | length) == d.atoms.zero or lookup('ansible.builtin.vars', c.value.var) != cw.v -%}{%- set cp.bad = cp.bad + [c.key] -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- if (cp.bad | length) > d.atoms.zero -%}{{ d.diagnostics[d.diagnostics.companion ~ d.diagnostics.joiner ~ (cp.bad | to_json)] }}{%- endif -%}
{%- set cu = namespace(p=root, links=d.atoms.empty_list) -%}
{%- for c in d.registry_rel.split(d.separator) -%}{%- set cu.p = cu.p ~ d.separator ~ c -%}{%- if cu.p is link -%}{%- set cu.links = cu.links + [c] -%}{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}
{%- if (cu.links | length) > d.atoms.zero or cu.p is not file -%}{{ d.diagnostics[d.diagnostics.custody ~ d.diagnostics.joiner ~ ([d.registry_rel, cu.links] | to_json)] }}{%- endif -%}
{%- if cu.p is vaulted_file -%}{{ d.diagnostics[d.diagnostics.vault ~ d.diagnostics.joiner ~ ([d.registry_rel] | to_json)] }}{%- endif -%}
{%- set text = lookup('ansible.builtin.file', cu.p, rstrip=d.atoms.false_value, lstrip=d.atoms.false_value) -%}
{%- if text is search(d.capture.undecodable_regex) -%}{{ d.diagnostics[d.diagnostics.undecodable ~ d.diagnostics.joiner ~ ([d.registry_rel] | to_json)] }}{%- endif -%}
{%- set actual = text | hash(d.digest.algorithm) -%}
{%- if actual != ex.v -%}{{ d.diagnostics[d.diagnostics.mismatch ~ d.diagnostics.joiner ~ ([d.registry_rel, ex.v, actual] | to_json)] }}{%- endif -%}
{%- set reg = namespace(n=(text | lme_doc_admit_text(parse, d.registry_rel))) -%}
{%- for k in d.registry_root -%}{%- set reg.n = reg.n[k] -%}{%- endfor -%}
{%- set pc = namespace(n=reg.n) -%}
{%- for k in d.parse_at -%}{%- set pc.n = pc.n[k] -%}{%- endfor -%}
{%- if (pc.n | to_json(**d.canonical_json)) != (parse | to_json(**d.canonical_json)) -%}{{ d.diagnostics[d.diagnostics.parse_contract ~ d.diagnostics.joiner ~ (d.parse_at | to_json)] }}{%- endif -%}
{%- set pr = namespace(names=d.protected_extra, bad=d.atoms.empty_list) -%}
{%- for l in d.protected_lists -%}
{%- if reg.n[l] is not sequence or reg.n[l] is string or reg.n[l] is mapping or (reg.n[l] | length) == d.atoms.zero -%}{%- set pr.bad = pr.bad + [l] -%}
{%- else -%}{%- set pr.names = pr.names + reg.n[l] -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- if (pr.bad | length) > d.atoms.zero -%}{{ d.diagnostics[d.diagnostics.lists ~ d.diagnostics.joiner ~ (pr.bad | to_json)] }}{%- endif -%}
{%- set cr = d.companions | dict2items | map(attribute='value') | map(attribute='var') | select('in', pr.names) | list -%}
{%- if (cr | length) > d.atoms.zero -%}{{ d.diagnostics[d.diagnostics.companion_reserved ~ d.diagnostics.joiner ~ (cr | to_json)] }}{%- endif -%}
{%- set pinned = pr.names | select('in', supplied) | list -%}
{%- if (pinned | length) > d.atoms.zero -%}{{ d.diagnostics[d.diagnostics.pinned ~ d.diagnostics.joiner ~ (pinned | to_json)] }}{%- endif -%}
{%- set ri = namespace(n=reg.n) -%}
{%- for k in d.reader_inputs.at -%}{%- set ri.n = ri.n[k] -%}{%- endfor -%}
{%- if ri.n is not mapping or (d.reader_inputs.roles | reject('in', ri.n) | list | length) > d.atoms.zero -%}{{ d.diagnostics[d.diagnostics.reader_inputs ~ d.diagnostics.joiner ~ (d.reader_inputs.at | join(d.diagnostics.joiner))] }}{%- endif -%}
{%- set rv = d.reader_inputs.roles | map('extract', ri.n) | list -%}
{%- set en = namespace(n=reg.n) -%}
{%- for k in d.reader_inputs.disjoint_from -%}{%- set en.n = en.n[k] -%}{%- endfor -%}
{%- if en.n is not mapping or (en.n.values() | reject('mapping') | list | length) > d.atoms.zero -%}{{ d.diagnostics[d.diagnostics.reader_inputs ~ d.diagnostics.joiner ~ (d.reader_inputs.disjoint_from | join(d.diagnostics.joiner))] }}{%- endif -%}
{%- set ev = en.n.values() | map('dict2items') | flatten(levels=1) | map(attribute='value') | list -%}
{%- if (rv | reject('string') | list | length) > d.atoms.zero or (rv | unique | list | length) != (rv | length) or (rv | reject('in', reg.n[d.reader_inputs.reserved_in]) | list | length) > d.atoms.zero or (rv | select('in', reg.n[d.reader_inputs.refused_in]) | list | length) > d.atoms.zero or (ev | reject('string') | list | length) > d.atoms.zero or (rv | select('in', ev) | list | length) > d.atoms.zero -%}{{ d.diagnostics[d.diagnostics.reader_inputs ~ d.diagnostics.joiner ~ (d.reader_inputs.at | join(d.diagnostics.joiner))] }}{%- endif -%}
{#- op1d: the carrier word and, under the projector carrier only, the admitted entry identity -#}
{{ dict([[d.output.identity, ex.v], [d.output.transport, sn.v], [d.output.ingress, d], [d.output.slice, reg.n[d.slice]], [d.output.reader_inputs, dict(d.reader_inputs.roles | zip(rv))],
         [d.output.carrier, (d.carriers.words.projector if px else d.carriers.words.envelope)]]
        + ([[d.output.entry_identity, pi.v]] if px else d.atoms.empty_list)) | tojson }}
{%- endmacro -%}
{#- records-c1-framework-31 (codex-tick824 A7-PROTECTED-NAME-HOME): the caller-protected top-level names, derived from
    the ingress declaration d (no roster): each companion var, then the envelope transport var, joined by
    d.caller_protected.joiner. Envelope-internal paths are not names; no other transport var is included.
    op1f (C1 s13 decl :120-121; CPL-SR918R-ROUTE-CALLER-PROTECTED): + the external X2 admission var
    (d.carriers.projector.admission.var); MAIN supplies it in the X2-admitted vector, an operator extra-var naming it
    refuses at the consumer; it is NOT a reserved output. -#}
{%- macro caller_protected(d) -%}
{{- ((d.companions | dict2items | map(attribute='value') | map(attribute='var') | list) + [d.transports[d.envelope_transport].var, d.carriers.projector.admission.var]) | join(d.caller_protected.joiner) -}}
{%- endmacro -%}
